# Safe default env_file: a fresh checkout can start without creating a secret file.
# For API authentication, copy this to .env, uncomment a key and set its value,
# then run: WORKERS_DEV_ENV_FILE=.env iii compose --up
# Keys must reach llm-router, which resolves provider credentials in its process.
# Never put real credentials in this tracked file.

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Alternatively, provider-openai-codex can use an existing Codex CLI login
# from ~/.codex/auth.json. No API key is needed for that provider.
